{#
    Customer testimonials — merchant-placeable component (home + builder pages).

    Two sources, one grid — the arrangement onyx settled on. Real reviews come
    from GET /api/storefront/reviews, the store-wide endpoint that already
    existed and that owns both the enable_reviews switch and the per-review
    review_visible opt-in; <custom-falak-testimonials> fetches them and builds
    the same .testimonial-card figures this template writes, so a quote looks
    the same whichever source it came from. Manual mode renders merchant-typed
    items so a brand-new store still has something to show. A block saved
    before `source` existed has nothing stored and falls into the manual
    branch, keeping the cards it always had.

    | Variable                  | Type    | Description                         |
    | component.title           | ?string | section title, localized server-side |
    | component.source          | ?string | reviews | manual (absent = manual)  |
    | component.limit           | ?int    | reviews mode: how many to fetch     |
    | component.items[].name    | string  |                                     |
    | component.show_stars      | ?bool   | whether the star row renders at all |
    | component.items[].stars   | int     | 1..5                                |
    | component.items[].text    | string  | localized server-side               |
    | position                  | int     |                                     |

    Customizer bindings — full rules in README, "Customizer annotations".
    | Element           | Tag                                             |
    | h2.block__title   | data-falak-field="title"                        |
    | figure.testimonial-card | data-falak-field="items" data-falak-bind="none" |

    `items` is a collection — see bind="none" in the README.

    Styleable parts: `stars`, `quote`, `author` inside each card; the card
    itself is styled through its data-falak-field="items" tag.
#}
<section class="block block--testimonials" id="testimonials-{{ position }}" {{ falak_section() }}>
    <div class="container">
        {% if component.title %}
            <h2 class="block__title" data-falak-field="title" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.title') }}">{{ component.title }}</h2>
        {% endif %}

        {#
            Absent means shown: a testimonials block placed before this switch
            existed has no `show_stars` saved, and should keep the stars it had.
        #}
        {% set show_stars = component.show_stars is defined ? component.show_stars : true %}

        {% if component.source == 'reviews' %}
            {# Fetched client-side: a home block gets no page data and the
               sandbox exposes no reviews function. The element hides the whole
               section — heading and all — when the store has nothing approved
               to show, rather than printing "no reviews yet" on a shop's home
               page. #}
            <custom-falak-testimonials
                limit="{{ component.limit|default(6) }}"
                {% if show_stars %}show-stars{% endif %}></custom-falak-testimonials>
        {% else %}
        <div class="testimonials-grid">
            {% for item in component.items %}
                <figure class="testimonial-card" data-falak-field="items" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.items') }}" data-falak-bind="none">
                    {#
                        The switch governs the whole grid, so it is read here
                        rather than per row. `range(1, 0)` counts DOWN to 1 and
                        would print a star for a rating of zero, which is why
                        the count is guarded as well as the switch.
                    #}
                    {% if show_stars and item.stars > 0 %}
                        <div class="testimonial-card__stars" data-falak-part="stars" aria-label="{{ item.stars }}/5">
                            {% for i in range(1, item.stars) %}★{% endfor %}
                        </div>
                    {% endif %}
                    <blockquote data-falak-part="quote">{{ item.text }}</blockquote>
                    <figcaption data-falak-part="author">{{ item.name }}</figcaption>
                </figure>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</section>
